questions.workedExample:
1. `read(fd, buf, 65536)` means *up to* 65,536 bytes.
2. For sockets the kernel returns whatever is in the receive buffer right now: here 1,200 bytes (about one TCP segment's worth).
3. The rest will arrive in later segments.
4. Correct pattern:

```c
size_t got = 0;
while (got < len) {
  ssize_t n = read(fd, buf + got,
                   len - got);
  if (n == 0) break;   /* EOF */
  if (n < 0) {
    if (errno == EINTR) continue;
    return -1;
  }
  got += n;
}
```

The `EINTR` check handles a signal interrupting the call.

